# VITISH 2026 · PS#99 SHM — hosted public demo environment (SEC-ON surface).
#
# COPY to `deploy/hosted-demo/.env.public` (git-ignored) and fill in the
# generated secrets.  Every value here is the SEC-REQUIRED public posture from
# scripts/verify_gate.sh gate 23 and docs/COMPREHENSIVE-ANALYSIS.md §2.1:
#
#   SEC-01  broker secure mode (user/pass, allow_anonymous=false, ACL)
#   SEC-02  demo route token-gated (route 403 when VITISH_DEMO_TOKEN unset)
#   SEC-03  WS origin validation — exact origins, never wildcard
#   SEC-04  Postgres bound to localhost (never the public interface)
#   SEC-06  CORS origins pinned to the exact public origin
#
# ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  NONE OF THESE SECRETS MAY BE COMMITTED.  `deploy/hosted-demo/.env.public` │
# │  is gitignored.  Generate passwords with `openssl rand -base64 24`.        │
# └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# --- broker (SEC-01): generated credentials — the ONLY identity that may WRITE.
# The mosquitto entrypoint (docker-compose.yml) turns the pair into a real
# SHA-512 password file + allow_anonymous false + the topic ACL, so the public
# broker rejects anonymous and read-only-defaults.  Keep this pair OUT of the
# committed twin build (it rides in VITISH_* at container runtime instead).
VITISH_MQTT_USER=vitish
VITISH_MQTT_PASS=REPLACE_openssl_rand_base64_24

# --- demo route (SEC-02): generated shared secret for POST /api/demo/scenario.
# The twin NEVER calls this route (it is operator-paced); the automated
# smoke/verify scripts use it.  Set it, or the route stays 403.
VITISH_DEMO_TOKEN=REPLACE_openssl_rand_base64_24

# --- bind: the API + WS must face the public interface (Caddy reverse-proxies
# 127.0.0.1:8000, but expose 8000/8765 to the container network).  The EXPOSED
# ports still require the Caddy origin gate below.
VITISH_API_HOST=0.0.0.0
VITISH_WS_HOST=0.0.0.0

# --- origins (SEC-03 / SEC-06): pinned to the exact public origin(s), never *
# or a bare port.  A browser at https://demo.example.com sends Origin:
# https://demo.example.com — anything else is rejected by the WS bridge and
# excluded from CORS.  Add the www./staging origin as a comma-separated list if
# you have one.
VITISH_WS_ORIGINS=https://demo.example.com
VITISH_CORS_ORIGINS=https://demo.example.com

# --- twin build-time (VITE_*): baked into the hosted twin so it connects to
# the SAME origin (the backend serves twin/dist under /twin).  With these set,
# the twin NEVER walks 127.0.0.1 (which in a visitor's browser would be THEIR
# laptop).  Build with docker compose build --build-arg or `cd twin && VITE_API_BASE=/api VITE_WS_URL=wss://demo.example.com/ws npm run build`.
VITE_API_BASE=/api
VITE_WS_URL=wss://demo.example.com/ws